# MASTER DEVELOPMENT PROMPT: ELIM WATER CORPORATE WEBSITE, ONLINE ORDERING AND ERP INTEGRATION PLATFORM

## ROLE AND DEVELOPMENT EXPECTATIONS

Act as a senior full-stack software architect, senior frontend engineer, backend engineer, database architect, UI/UX designer and ERP integration specialist with extensive experience building enterprise-grade business applications.

Your assignment is to design, develop, integrate, test and deploy a complete, modern, responsive corporate website and online customer ordering platform for **Elim Water**.

This is an extension of an EXISTING Elim Water Factory ERP that is already built and actively used.

You MUST integrate the new website with the existing ERP. Do not create a disconnected ordering system, duplicate inventory system or a separate database that cannot communicate with the ERP.

The objective is to provide Elim Water with:

1. A professional corporate website.
2. A comprehensive product catalogue.
3. Online customer booking and ordering.
4. A secure order management dashboard.
5. An assigned staff member responsible for attending to bookings.
6. Dispatch and delivery management.
7. Customer communication and order status tracking.
8. Real-time or appropriately synchronised ERP integration.
9. Centralised reporting and business visibility.

The implementation must be production-ready, secure, maintainable, scalable and suitable for real factory operations.

